></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T01:12:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134602009,imgsize-1807006.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kathua fratricide: Plaint over bringing child to project site enraged killer]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kathua-fratricide-plaint-over-bringing-child-to-project-site-enraged-killer/articleshow/134601137.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134601137.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Accused remanded in police custody for 7 days; DG visits spot]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kathua-fratricide-plaint-over-bringing-child-to-project-site-enraged-killer/articleshow/134601137.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kathua-fratricide-plaint-over-bringing-child-to-project-site-enraged-killer/articleshow/134601137.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T00:25:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sanjay Khajuria</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134601376,imgsize-20906.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[J&amp;K parties, barring BJP, blast top officials for letter to assembly against statehood resolution]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jk-parties-barring-bjp-blast-top-officials-for-letter-to-assembly-against-statehood-resolution/articleshow/134601139.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134601139.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jk-parties-barring-bjp-blast-top-officials-for-letter-to-assembly-against-statehood-resolution/articleshow/134601139.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jk-parties-barring-bjp-blast-top-officials-for-letter-to-assembly-against-statehood-resolution/articleshow/134601139.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T00:21:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Naseer Ganai</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134601316,imgsize-381530.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Gadkari announces Rs 1,176 cr 6-lane bridge over Teesta]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/gadkari-announces-rs-1176-cr-6-lane-bridge-over-teesta/articleshow/134600035.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134600035.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a major development, the Indian government has greenlit funding for the construction of a bridge over the Teesta river in Darjeeling, set to strengthen connections between Sikkim and North-Eastern states as well as the vital Siliguri Corridor. Alongside this is an expressway from Gorakhpur to Siliguri, promising to enhance regional collaboration and economic progress.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/gadkari-announces-rs-1176-cr-6-lane-bridge-over-teesta/articleshow/134600035.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/gadkari-announces-rs-1176-cr-6-lane-bridge-over-teesta/articleshow/134600035.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T23:14:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dipak K Dash</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134600137,imgsize-79870.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Cabinet clears Rs 1,789cr intelligent traffic system for Delhi, first planned before 2010 CWG]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cabinet-clears-rs-1789cr-intelligent-traffic-system-for-delhi-first-planned-before-2010-cwg/articleshow/134599851.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134599851.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Union Cabinet has approved a Rs 1,789 crore Intelligent Traffic Management System project for Delhi. This project will feature AI-enabled traffic signals and real-time congestion detection across key corridors. The system aims to enhance traffic management by integrating existing signals, CCTVs, and AI technology. It will improve the movement of emergency vehicles and assist in identifying traffic violations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cabinet-clears-rs-1789cr-intelligent-traffic-system-for-delhi-first-planned-before-2010-cwg/articleshow/134599851.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cabinet-clears-rs-1789cr-intelligent-traffic-system-for-delhi-first-planned-before-2010-cwg/articleshow/134599851.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T22:54:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dipak K Dash and Raj Shekhar Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134599851,imgsize-285378.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Govt invites global mining majors to first India Mining Week in Nov]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/govt-invites-global-mining-majors-to-first-india-mining-week-in-nov/articleshow/134599688.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134599688.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In November 2026, India is set to host its inaugural India Mining Week, aiming to foster global engagement and investment in the mining sector. This significant event will spotlight policy advancements and the discussion of essential minerals, featuring a high-profile conference, various exhibitions, and dialogues on mining technology and sustainability.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/govt-invites-global-mining-majors-to-first-india-mining-week-in-nov/articleshow/134599688.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/govt-invites-global-mining-majors-to-first-india-mining-week-in-nov/articleshow/134599688.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T22:44:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Atul Mathur</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134599755,imgsize-72866.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[NHAI to inspect 17 highways awarded at 15% below estimates]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/nhai-to-inspect-17-highways-awarded-at-15-below-estimates/articleshow/134599299.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134599299.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The National Highways Authority of India (NHAI) is set to implement special inspections on 17 highway projects that were awarded at least 15 per cent below the estimated costs. These inspections aim to uphold quality standards and will begin with initial reviews by December, followed by further checks in six months. Teams of seasoned engineers will oversee the inspections, and any quality inconsistencies will be rectified in line with contractual obligations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/nhai-to-inspect-17-highways-awarded-at-15-below-estimates/articleshow/134599299.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/nhai-to-inspect-17-highways-awarded-at-15-below-estimates/articleshow/134599299.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T22:27:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dipak K Dash</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134599494,imgsize-156164.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Protests against SIR, CEC: Is it time for Congress and INDIA bloc to take a leaf out of CJP's playbook?]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/protests-against-sir-cec-is-it-time-for-congress-and-india-bloc-to-take-a-leaf-out-of-cjps-playbook/articleshow/134597912.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134597912.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The INDIA bloc, under Congress's leadership, is gearing up for a vigorous campaign against electoral misconduct and the Election Commission's authority. Their strategy includes widespread protests and a pivotal 'Save Democracy March' to elevate public consciousness while pressuring for essential reforms. Additionally, the bloc intends to approach the Supreme Court about ongoing electoral challenges. Among their key proposals are reinstating ballot voting and refining voter registration methods.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/protests-against-sir-cec-is-it-time-for-congress-and-india-bloc-to-take-a-leaf-out-of-cjps-playbook/articleshow/134597912.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/protests-against-sir-cec-is-it-time-for-congress-and-india-bloc-to-take-a-leaf-out-of-cjps-playbook/articleshow/134597912.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T21:34:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Kunal Varma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134598750,imgsize-120940.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Certificate not needed’: JD(U)’s sharp reply to Sonia Gandhi on Nitish]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/certificate-not-needed-jdus-sharp-reply-to-sonia-gandhi-on